Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.480
Yesterday, during the press briefing of&nbsp;
a White House press secretary, Jen Psaki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.600
there was a clarification about Joe&nbsp;
Biden's tax plan when Joe Biden said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:18.880
nobody earning under four hundred thousand&nbsp;
dollars a year will see an increase in taxes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:26.480
Did Joe Biden mean individuals earning up to&nbsp;
400 K or did Joe Biden mean households earning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.440
up to four hundred K? During yesterday's&nbsp;
press briefing, Jen Psaki clarified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.840
that it means households that is different than&nbsp;
four hundred thousand dollars per person. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.920
four hundred thousand dollars per household.&nbsp;
And within moments on Fox News, right wing host&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:51.760
Charles Payne, as well as Republican Senator Chuck&nbsp;
Grassley, we're saying, look, look, we told you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:59.520
Joe Biden is coming for middle income people.&nbsp;
Take a look at this clip. So what are we doing?&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:05.120
The exact opposite way. We know taxes were&nbsp;
promised and elections have consequences. But I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.600
don't think anyone thought that the president,&nbsp;
president President Biden was talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.880
household making. Four hundred thousand. I always&nbsp;
tell people, Senator, be careful when you pick up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.640
the torching of pitchforks. Sooner or later&nbsp;
you might get. Up in front of your own house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:25.040
the middle income people of this country are smart&nbsp;
enough to know that when they hear a politician&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.480
or even the president of United States say that&nbsp;
only high income people, the very wealthiest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:38.800
are going pay the tax, they know better, if you&nbsp;
go there, you're going to eventually end up paying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:45.200
taxes on middle income people.
So there are two relevant parts here. First is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:54.240
is 400000 dollars as a household income? Is that&nbsp;
middle income? That's the first question. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.920
second question is, are these the folks we should&nbsp;
be targeting for higher taxes? So when you say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:06.400
400000 for a household, that could be two people&nbsp;
making two hundred K each, that could be someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:13.200
makes one seventy five and someone makes 25. Could&nbsp;
be, you know, three fifty and fifty total. Four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:20.000
hundred thousand. That puts you in the top two&nbsp;
percent of households in the United States. So by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.880
definition you're not in the middle. If you're&nbsp;
in the top two percent now, you could say, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:34.080
you're in the middle like, you know, anything&nbsp;
that goes down to the second percentile and up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:40.160
to the 90th counts middle. And then you've got two&nbsp;
percent of people that are poor and two percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.160
of people that are rich. I don't think most&nbsp;
people would imagine that the meat of the curve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.920
is the middle 98 percent, for example,&nbsp;
or the middle 96 percent. By definition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.280
if you're in the top two percent, you're not in&nbsp;
the middle income. Now, you can go and look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:59.680
this for yourself. If you go to dequeue. Why D.J.&nbsp;
Dotcom? You can type in any household income. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.960
you type in four hundred thousand, for example,&nbsp;
you will see you're in the 90th percentile, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:11.120
top to get into the top two percent. This is 20&nbsp;
19 data to get into the top two percent. You had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:15.920
to make as a household three hundred and eighty&nbsp;
seven thousand dollars. It's a little higher now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.400
probably because of inflation. It's right around&nbsp;
four hundred thousand a year. Puts you in the top&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:27.520
two percent. Now, the second part is actually more&nbsp;
interesting to me. You can like they're just wrong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:32.000
that four hundred K is middle income. You're in&nbsp;
the top two percent. The more interesting part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.840
is you can absolutely make the case that we should&nbsp;
be targeting not people who as individuals might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.240
only make two hundred thousand as part of a four&nbsp;
hundred thousand dollar household. You should be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.360
looking at people that are making five million&nbsp;
a year, 20 million a year, 200 million a year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:53.760
the billionaires that there's so much more meat&nbsp;
on the bone there that you shouldn't even include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.800
four hundred thousand dollar households right now.&nbsp;
Now, that is a valid argument in the sense that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.920
you're not denying reality. You're not saying four&nbsp;
hundred KS middle income. No, 400 K still in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.520
top two percent, but you should be targeting the&nbsp;
top one percent or the top zero point five percent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:15.120
or the top zero point two percent. Four hundred&nbsp;
thousand dollars is a lot of money in any city,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:21.120
but four hundred thousand in Manhattan with&nbsp;
three kids is nowhere near the same as four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:26.560
hundred thousand dollars as a couple with no&nbsp;
kids in Alabama. So you just open this up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:34.320
more debate potentially if you make this about ten&nbsp;
million a year and up or 20 million a year and up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:40.000
there's no debate in any city. Maybe if you&nbsp;
have a thousand kids. Right. But but in any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.680
city with one, two, three, four kids, that's a&nbsp;
ton of money anywhere. Maybe you start there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:52.640
And that is a different discussion and one that&nbsp;
certainly could be had. But there is no way to say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:05:01.120
Biden's coming for the middle class. By&nbsp;
starting tax increases at four hundred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.400
thousand dollars, it's just look&nbsp;
at a bell curve, it's not the case.&nbsp;&nbsp;

